#: ../../src/guide/threads.rst:49
msgid ""
"``uv_thread_t`` is just an alias for ``pthread_t`` on Unix, but this is "
"an implementation detail, avoid depending on it to always be true."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/guide/threads.rst:52
msgid ""
"The second parameter is the function which will serve as the entry point "
"for the thread, the last parameter is a ``void *`` argument which can be "
"used to pass custom parameters to the thread. The function ``hare`` will "
"now run in a separate thread, scheduled pre-emptively by the operating "
"system:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/guide/threads.rst:64
msgid ""
"Unlike ``pthread_join()`` which allows the target thread to pass back a "
"value to the calling thread using a second parameter, "
"``uv_thread_join()`` does not. To send values use :ref:`inter-thread-"
"communication`."
msgstr ""

